# Docker build-context excludes.
#
# Anything listed here is NOT sent to the Docker daemon. Since the Dockerfile
# now names every path it copies (there is no `COPY . /home/scripts/`), this
# file no longer decides what ends up in the image — the COPY instructions do.
# What it still does is keep the build context small and keep local, untracked
# working-tree files out of it entirely.
#
# Two exclusions remain load-bearing rather than cosmetic, because they sit
# inside a path the Dockerfile does copy (`COPY js/ /home/scripts/js/`):
#   js/tests/          — excluding it here is what keeps the suite out of the image
#   **/node_modules/   — stops a host-side node_modules from overwriting the
#                        builder's clean, prod-only copy

# Version control & local tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
.claude

# Usage examples — documentation only, never used at build or runtime
examples/

# Test sources and coverage artifacts — never executed inside the image
js/tests/
tests/
coverage/

# Dependencies: the runtime node_modules is produced by the builder stage
# (`npm ci --omit=dev`) and copied via `COPY --from=node-builder`. Excluding any
# host-side node_modules stops it from overwriting that clean, prod-only copy.
**/node_modules/

# Dev-only helper script (release notes generation)
generate-release-notes.sh

# Local, untracked working notes (gitignored). Kept out of the build context so
# a personal file present in a maintainer's tree is never sent to the daemon.
notes.md

# OS / editor / log cruft
.DS_Store
*.log
*.swp
